  "details": "Currently Group+ instances act like Friends+ instances. However I would much prefer if we got Group+ instances that act like Invite+ instances.\n\n- Group+ currently: Group members and friends of group members can see and freely join the instance.\n\n- Group Invite+ as I would want it: Group members can see and freely join the instance, but people in the instance can only accept invite requests. They cannot invite people directly nor can the instance be seen for non-group-members. (Just like invite+).\n\nThe use case for this would be if for instance you had a some friends who are all part of a group; They could see and freely join this new instance type, but friends/acquaintances of those members would have to request to join the instance. Which prevents the instance population from ballooning out of proportion and essentially ending up like a public instance (which so often happens with friends+ instances). A regular Group (non-plus) instance does not suffice because it completely prevents non-members from requesting invites and being temporarily allowed in.",
